    "title": "Homecoming homer for Ivan Melendez, Chihuahuas walk off Aces 13-11 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Sam Guzman No media credit provided. ,\n1 hours ago\nEL PASO, Texas (KTSM) — El Paso native Ivan Melendez went yard in his hometown Wednesday against the El Paso Chihuahuas.\nIn the second game of his homecoming series, Melendez delivered a solo home run to center field to help the Triple-A Reno Aces tie the game at 11-11 in the top of the eighth inning. It marked his second homer of the season.\nThe game went into extra innings, and in the bottom of the 10th, Nick Schnell connected on a two-run home run to center field to lift the Chihuahuas to a 13-11 walk-off win in Game 2 of the series.\nGame 3 of the series is Thursday at Southwest University Park. First pitch is scheduled for 6:35 p.m.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KTSM 9 News.",
    "summary": "By Sam Guzman No media credit provided. In the second game of his homecoming series, Melendez delivered a solo home run to center field to help the Triple-A Reno Aces tie the game at 11-11 in the top of the eighth inning. The game went into extra innings, and in the bottom of the 10th, Nick Schnell connected on a two-run home run to center field to lift the Chihuahuas to a 13-11 walk-off win in Game 2 of the series. Game 3 of the series is Thursday at Southwest University Park. Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved.",
